 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Pre-visualization time is proportional to the number of surface vertices, the number of observation lines per vertex, and the number of samples per ray. It is slightly greater than conventional DVR visualization time for small cone counts (e.g., 3 cones, 8 lines) but increases with more cones [S1, unofficial]. Rendering time is fast, comparable to conventional surface rendering, as it involves only dot products and face averaging [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Memory usage is proportional to the number of surface vertices and the number of observation lines. For a dataset with 8 cones per vertex and 8 lines per cone, memory usage was close to 32 MB for a small dataset (86x42x59) [S1, unofficial].
